    "title": "UMass football announces 2026 kickoff times and broadcast details",
    "text": "Massachusetts football will open the 2026 season against Rutgers at 6 p.m. on Thursday, Sept. 3 at SHI Stadium in Piscataway, New Jersey, with the game set to be broadcast on the Big Ten Network, according to a May 27 announcement.\nKickoff times for the first two home games have also been confirmed. The Minutemen will face Sacred Heart on Saturday, Sept. 12 and Stonehill on Saturday, Sept. 19, both starting at 3:30 p.m. These games will be available for viewing on ESPN+.\nThe university said that its matchup against UConn has been rescheduled from Saturday, Oct. 24 to Friday, Oct. 23, with a new kickoff time of 7 p.m., airing on CBS Sports Network. Additionally, Massachusetts will play Bowling Green at noon on Saturday, Nov. 28.\nFor November matchups associated with Mid-American Conference action (#Maction), specific game times and networks are yet to be finalized but are expected to air either at 7 or 7:30 p.m., with coverage options including ESPN2, ESPNU or CBS Sports Network.\nThe university stated that all remaining game times and television assignments will be announced twelve days prior to each scheduled date. Games throughout the season may air across ESPN platforms (ESPN/ESPN2/ESPNU/ESPN+) and CBS Sports Network.",
    "summary": "Massachusetts football will open the 2026 season against Rutgers at 6 p.m. on Thursday, Sept. 3 at SHI Stadium in Piscataway, New Jersey, with the game set to be broadcast on the Big Ten Network, according to a May 27 announcement. The university said that its matchup against UConn has been rescheduled from Saturday, Oct. 24 to Friday, Oct. 23, with a new kickoff time of 7 p.m., airing on CBS Sports Network.",
